Apply UpdateColumnNullability in the CDC schema-evolution path.

Since Paimon 1.2, NestedSchemaUtils.generateNestedColumnUpdates emits the
nullability of a type change as its own UpdateColumnNullability. 1.1.1
carried it inside UpdateColumnType. UpdatedDataFieldsProcessFunctionBase
has no branch for it, so a column whose type and nullability change
together throws "Unsupported schema change class" and kills the job.
Upstream 1.4.2 has the same gap.

Moved from getlago/lago-infrastructure#2220 (review finding). EvolveTest
step 7 in images/flink-paimon/test covers it.

diff --git a/paimon-flink/paimon-flink-cdc/src/main/java/org/apache/paimon/flink/sink/cdc/UpdatedDataFieldsProcessFunctionBase.java b/paimon-flink/paimon-flink-cdc/src/main/java/org/apache/paimon/flink/sink/cdc/UpdatedDataFieldsProcessFunctionBase.java
--- a/paimon-flink/paimon-flink-cdc/src/main/java/org/apache/paimon/flink/sink/cdc/UpdatedDataFieldsProcessFunctionBase.java
+++ b/paimon-flink/paimon-flink-cdc/src/main/java/org/apache/paimon/flink/sink/cdc/UpdatedDataFieldsProcessFunctionBase.java
